      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For symptomatic deficiencies like interveinal chlorosis, both foliar applications and soil amendments are viable options, and the choice depends on the severity and persistence of the issue. Foliar sprays provide a quick, temporary supplement by directly delivering soluble nutrients to the leaves, which is good for immediate symptom relief. Conversely, amending the soil with acidifying materials, such as elemental sulfur or acidifying $\\text{N}$ fertilizers, can slowly lower the $\\text{pH}$ to improve long-term nutrient mobility.",
